### Opt-5: REVERTED (2026-06-29)

The 2-group skip caused jit-cache=full correctness failures. Root cause:
SubqueryPreparer::MergeSubquery uses unordered_map<idx_t, unique_ptr<LogicalOperator>>
and unordered_set<idx_t> (subquery_preparer.cpp:470-471, 538-539, 569, 610).
Non-deterministic iteration order produces different expression bindings between
benchmark iterations, causing JIT cache hash collisions with mismatched types.

Error: "Failed to cast expression to type - expression type mismatch" on query
10c with jit-cache=full (12 total failures across all jit-cache=full configs).

Attempted fixes:
1. has_prior_temps_ guard: only apply 2-group skip at initial iteration (no prior
   temp tables). Passes correctness but regresses performance (+8.5% vs +4.9%).
   73 queries that hit 2-group at later iterations lose the skip.
2. Decision: fully revert. Net improvement was only 69ms (measured with 15 warm
   runs using correct parser). Not worth the complexity or DuckDB-side fix.

Files modified (revert):
- src/split/node_based_splitter.cpp: Removed 2-group skip block and
  has_prior_temps_ usage
- include/split/node_based_splitter.h: Removed has_prior_temps_ field

